  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Syria Regional Appeal - Lebanon - Education in Emergencies</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Syria Regional Appeal - Lebanon - Education in Emergencies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, UNRWA will continue to provide educational services to Palestine refugee students, including around 5,000 PRS children,  as well as 718 students in vocational training courses. 
The socioeconomic and health conditions in Lebanon have caused immense psychological distress for children. The continued availability of psychosocial support services (PSS) remains crucial to improve children&#x2019;s social and emotional learning, and to build their psychosocial resilience by providing them with the tools needed to cope with shocks and stress. In 20213, school counsellors will continue to provide individual and group counselling, awareness sessions for both children and caregivers, as well as parenting skills sessions. UNRWA also aims to continue tackling youth challenges through enhancing the quality of vocational education. UNRWA will continue to support the enrolment of PRS and PRL students in various trade and semi-professional vocational courses at STC.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, UNRWA will continue to provide educational services to Palestine refugee students, including around 5,000 PRS children,  as well as 718 students in vocational training courses. 
The socioeconomic and health conditions in Lebanon have caused immense psychological distress for children. The continued availability of psychosocial support services (PSS) remains crucial to improve children&#x2019;s social and emotional learning, and to build their psychosocial resilience by providing them with the tools needed to cope with shocks and stress. In 20213, school counsellors will continue to provide individual and group counselling, awareness sessions for both children and caregivers, as well as parenting skills sessions. UNRWA also aims to continue tackling youth challenges through enhancing the quality of vocational education. UNRWA will continue to support the enrolment of PRS and PRL students in various trade and semi-professional vocational courses at STC.</narrative>
  </description>
